# .env.example — generated by `aislang plan`
#
# Lists every env var your resolved provider stack will
# consult at runtime. Copy this file to `.env` (gitignored),
# fill in the values, and `docker compose up` reads them.
#
# Sources (merged + alphabetized):
#   - provider credentials derived from resolved models
#   - `secret` blocks with `env://` URIs (user-declared)
#
# Catalog version: 2026-05-25
#
# Recommended .gitignore entry:
#   .env
#
# aislang itself never reads a real `.env` — secrets are the
# user's responsibility, handed to docker compose at runtime.

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OLLAMA_API_BASE=

# --- Ollama-on-host hint ---
# If you run Ollama as a container (or native binary) on this
# same machine with port 11434 published, set the value above to
#   http://host.docker.internal:11434
# The compose stack wires `host.docker.internal` to the host
# gateway so this URL resolves uniformly on Mac, Windows, and Linux.
